  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "The shortest distance between the lines&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mn>0</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is equal to ______",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "14",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given equations are</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is passing through a point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and it&#39;s direction ratios are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p><p>So,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p>And,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mn>0</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is passing through a point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and it&#39;s direction ratios are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p>Now,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>14</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#215;</mo><msub><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mtd><mtd><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mtd><mtd><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#215;</mo><msub><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p>So,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#215;</mo><msub><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>16</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>36</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>144</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn></math></p><p>We know that the shortest distance between two skew lines is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><msub><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#215;</mo><msub><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#215;</mo><msub><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>14</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mn>14</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>168</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>14</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn></math>&nbsp;units</p>",
